22. Complete Algorithmic Trading Workflow
1. Form a clear trading hypothesis.
2. Collect and validate historical data.
3. Define objective entry and exit rules.
4. Implement position sizing and risk limits.
5. Build a realistic backtest.
6. Include fees, slippage and execution constraints.
7. Evaluate returns, drawdowns and risk metrics.
8. Test for biases and overfitting.
9. Validate with out-of-sample and walk-forward tests.
10. Paper trade and verify execution behavior.
11. Deploy only after operational and risk checks.
12. Monitor, audit and periodically reassess the strategy.
